vaporOS nuttx-apps patch: termcurses-read-retry

Problem:   termcurses_getkeycode() returns -1 when read() returns no data (a
           non-blocking fd, or VMIN=0), and callers (vi) retry immediately.
Evidence:  vi hung the USB console. CAUTION: the real cause of that hang
           was the CDC-ACM race (nuttx/cdcacm-tx-ring-race.patch). Tasks here are
           round-robin (SCHED_RR), so a spinning vi should not starve the others; this patch
           was a wrong guess that happens to be harmless. It is kept only because
           an empty-read busy loop is bad on its own.
Fix:       sleep 10 ms and retry on EAGAIN/EINTR/0-byte reads.
Upstream:  NO as is. Needs a demonstrated failure first; otherwise drop this
           patch.

diff --git a/system/termcurses/tcurses_vt100.c b/system/termcurses/tcurses_vt100.c
index ac4685a4e..20dca13ca 100644
--- a/system/termcurses/tcurses_vt100.c
+++ b/system/termcurses/tcurses_vt100.c
@@ -1193,6 +1193,19 @@ static int tcurses_vt100_getkeycode(FAR struct termcurses_s *dev,
           priv->keycount = read(fd, priv->keybuf, sizeof(priv->keybuf)-1);
           if (priv->keycount <= 0)
             {
+              /* vaporOS: a read that returns "no data" (non-blocking fd,
+               * VMIN=0) used to return -1 and callers retried at full
+               * speed, starving the USB/serial worker threads.  Wait a
+               * little and retry; only a real error ends the wait.
+               */
+
+              if (priv->keycount == 0 || errno == EAGAIN || errno == EINTR)
+                {
+                  priv->keycount = 0;
+                  usleep(10000);
+                  continue;
+                }
+
               return -1;
             }
 
